          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: أرز",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أرز — aruzz — \"rice\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أرز (aruzz) is an old loan. It is usually traced, probably by way of Aramaic, to Greek oryza, \"rice\" (EtymDB), a word the Greeks had from further east. Lane lists aruzz under ʾ-r-z as a well-known grain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
